      "room": "Monroe",
      "track": "Tech",
      "title": "Enabling Agentic Systems for Life Science Discovery",
      "presenter": "",
      "format": "",
      "authors": "Chris Dallago",
      "abstract": "AI in biology is rapidly evolving from isolated foundation models toward persistent, agent-driven scientific systems capable of reasoning, experimentation, and continuous improvement. This talk introduces NVIDIA BioNeMo as an AI Scientist Enablement Stack that integrates domain-specific models, scientific tools, accelerated data processing, and production deployment infrastructure into a unified platform for life science R&D. We will explore how agentic architectures can support workflows in protein design and genomics while enabling scalable design-test-learn loops. The session will conclude with a discussion of emerging trends in autonomous discovery systems and the future role of AI agents in computational biology research.",
      "dateLabel": "2026-07-14",
      "startLabel": "12:20",
      "endLabel": "13:00",
      "dayKey": "2026-07-14",
      "searchText": "2026-07-14 12:20:00 13:00:00 monroe tech enabling agentic systems for life science discovery chris dallago ai in biology is rapidly evolving from isolated foundation models toward persistent, agent-driven scientific systems capable of reasoning, experimentation, and continuous improvement. this talk introduces nvidia bionemo as an ai scientist enablement stack that integrates domain-specific models, scientific tools, accelerated data processing, and production deployment infrastructure into a unified platform for life science r&d. we will explore how agentic architectures can support workflows in protein design and genomics while enabling scalable design-test-learn loops. the session will conclude with a discussion of emerging trends in autonomous discovery systems and the future role of ai agents in computational biology research."
