      "title": "Computational Biology Career Opportunities in Industry and How to Prepare for Them!",
      "presenter": "",
      "format": "",
      "authors": "Ben Busby, Alexis Norris, Dan DeBlasio, Geraldine Van der Auwera, Theresa Wohlever",
      "abstract": "This panel will make grad students and postdocs aware of job roles available in industry, government and non-tenure track academia, as well as highlight training opportunities and networking strategies to increase the likelihood they will get those jobs. Each panelist will give a short talk on their job responsibilities and how they got there, followed by an audience-engaged Q&A session.",
