      "startLabel": "11:00",
      "endLabel": "11:20",
      "dayKey": "2026-07-16",
      "searchText": "2026-07-16 11:00:00 11:20:00 9-10 combo bioinformatics in the usa advancing bioinformatics and computational biology in the united states: funding priorities and opportunities from the national library of medicine catherine farrell catherine farrell the national library of medicine (nlm), one of the 27 institutes and centers of the u.s. national institutes of health (nih), plays a pivotal national role in advancing biomedical informatics, bioinformatics, and computational biology. nlm supports research that strengthens the u.s. biomedical data ecosystem, accelerates discovery, and expands the use of trustworthy, interoperable, and open access biomedical information resources. this presentation will highlight nlm's current research funding priorities, including rigorous and explainable ai, multi-omics data integration, scalable computational workflows, sustainable knowledge resources, and human centered tools. it will also introduce available funding opportunities across nlm's extramural portfolio and describe how these mechanisms support innovation in these areas. a central focus will be the newly released par-26-040 funding opportunity: advancing bioinformatics, translational bioinformatics, and computational biology research (r01). this opportunity supports groundbreaking, generalizable, and openly disseminated approaches in areas such as multi-omics analytics, complex biological data integration, benchmarking frameworks, and reproducible and interpretable ai and machine learning methods. the presentation will emphasize the importance of aligning proposals with agency priorities, including nlm's mission, the nih unified strategy, and department of health and human services priorities, and will highlight ai initiatives relevant to translational sciences. practical guidance will be provided on how the nih review process works, how proposals are evaluated, and how applicants can strengthen responsiveness to review criteria. attendees will gain a clear understanding of current funding pathways and emerging opportunities, as well as practical insight into accessing online guidance and tools that support the development of competitive applications."
